      "content": "That's an interesting take, but some economists and human rights groups argue that strict enforcement actually hurts the economy by creating labor shortages in key sectors and that the focus on sovereignty often overlooks the humanitarian obligations of the US. How would you reconcile those views with the points you just made?",
